WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:06.480
If you were here in August

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:07.550
and you were sitting on the beach,

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:09.140
on a blanket facing the sea,

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.700
you would think you were
in the Turks and Caicos

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.120
in the Caribbean.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.710
The beaches have been renamed

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:17.100
Spiagge Bianche in Italian,

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.340
which literally means "the white beaches"

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:22.236
and you'll see hundreds of beachgoers

00:00:22.236 --> 00:00:25.730
flocking to that
destination in the summers.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:27.468
Vogue Italia magazine

00:00:27.468 --> 00:00:30.360
put the white beaches on its cover.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.630
I mean, it's strikingly beautiful

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:36.000
but this sort of Caribbean-like oasis

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.913
also has a dirty secret.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.550
Well, here's this enormous chemical plant

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.450
on the beaches of Tuscany.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.070
And for over 100 years,

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:52.070
it has been pumping 24/7, 365 days a year

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:55.020
its discharge straight onto the coast

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.420
and into the coastal waters.

00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:59.040
It's visible on the beach,

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.310
it's visible from space even.

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:03.250
So much so that it has literally

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:05.380
transformed the landscape.

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:06.850
The beaches are now

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:08.790
a stark and bright white,

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.970
whereas all around that area

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.120
the beaches are sort
of a more beigy color.

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:16.900
And the question that came up is

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:19.353
how could that possibly be legal,

00:01:19.353 --> 00:01:20.560
that a chemical plant

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:22.170
can just take left over

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.020
and just pump it out into the sea?

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:26.690
And so we set out to answer that question,

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:28.060
you know, is it okay?

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:31.440
Is it damaging the environment
and hurting people?

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.750
And the answer was
actually more complicated

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.150
than we thought it would be.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:48.910
Solvay is a multinational
chemicals company

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:51.370
based in Brussels, Belgium.

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:52.870
It's got a market value

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:56.089
of far over 10 billion euros.

00:01:56.089 --> 00:01:58.523
Its operations are all around the world.

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:03.240
Well, here's a town, Rosignano Solvay,

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:04.940
which has the name suggests,

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:08.650
takes its name from the
company for a reason.

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:09.870
Over 100 years ago

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:12.660
when Solvay spotted this location

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.890
on the coast of Italy,

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:17.730
as infrastructure was
being built around it,

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:19.070
it found a location

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:20.610
which would be suitable

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:21.620
for its production

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:25.230
and literally built a
town around the plant.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.605
I mean we're talking schools,

00:02:26.605 --> 00:02:29.517
we're talking a hospital, a theater.

00:02:29.517 --> 00:02:31.598
So this town is literally

00:02:31.598 --> 00:02:33.810
the embodiment of the company

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:35.773
and its plant in Tuscany.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:38.960
This is a plant that makes soda ash,

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:40.280
an ingredient in glass

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:41.700
and it's used for other things.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:42.785
And essentially they take

00:02:42.785 --> 00:02:44.910
local limestone from quarries

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:46.960
and bring it in and pulverize it.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:48.060
What essentially,

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:50.100
what is being discharged are tiny,

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.788
tiny particles of limestone

00:02:52.788 --> 00:02:54.710
mixed in seawater.

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:56.660
And that is what is making

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:59.043
the beach in part that color.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:03.401
Their position is they take

00:03:03.401 --> 00:03:06.740
locally quarried, natural stone

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:08.190
and they put it through their plant.

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:11.500
And that the totally
natural sandy byproduct

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:12.820
is just pushed out to the sea

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:15.010
where it does a terrific job contributing

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:17.700
to the environment by helping the beach

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:20.020
not fall victim to erosion.

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:22.850
But the process itself of pulverizing

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:25.990
the stone unlocks natural metals,

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:28.793
minerals that are inside the stone.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:34.653
Arsenic, mercury, zinc, lead.

00:03:35.662 --> 00:03:38.440
Some of it is dissolved in the water

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:41.100
and some of it is still in particles,

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:44.580
in compounds that are part of the rock.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:47.570
And every year they pump the equivalent

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:52.150
of almost 250,000 tons

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:54.240
of these suspended solids

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:55.290
directly onto the beach

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.260
and into the Mediterranean.

00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:58.300
The Italian government,

00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:59.161
as they just have,

00:03:59.161 --> 00:04:01.640
reauthorized them with a new license,

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:03.160
they get their stamp of approval.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:06.703
And it seems there that life goes on.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:10.480
Except that we've been able

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.170
to answer part of the question about,

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:13.770
is it legal, should it be legal?

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:21.030
Well under Italian law,

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:22.800
the one legal standard the company

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:26.111
has to meet reflects the concentration

00:04:26.111 --> 00:04:28.570
of heavy metals in the discharge.

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:29.510
What that means is

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:32.600
it cannot exceed certain thresholds

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:36.482
of milligrams per liter of heavy metals

00:04:36.482 --> 00:04:38.253
in its discharge.

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:42.430
And it turns out that in 2013,

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:45.170
it had exceeded those
concentration limits.

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:46.940
And it never went to trial.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:49.210
It went to a plea bargain for polluting

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:50.580
the beach around the plant

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:53.510
and of diluting the effluent

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:55.180
in a way that disguised the fact

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:57.630
that they were exceeding legal limits

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.910
such as mercury that were going

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:01.650
directly into the Mediterranean.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:03.100
And this was a turning point.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.410
Solvay promised to the court that

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:09.760
it would somehow treat
for those heavy metals

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:11.903
to reduce the concentrations.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:35.840
The result was that Solvay

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:38.700
has not changed how it produces soda ash,

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:42.210
nor how it discharges the pollutants.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:44.560
It has simply relabeled

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:47.230
some of the plant's processes.

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:49.550
They're taking sea water,

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:52.050
which doesn't count to
their fraction normally

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:53.680
because it's just used to cool

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:54.780
all the hot stuff in the plants.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:56.200
It's not part of the production itself.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.240
It's cooling water comes in from the sea,

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:01.730
goes out, doesn't count
towards their concentration.

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:04.330
They built something in
treating for ammonia,

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:07.920
that routed about a third of this seawater

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:10.300
through a new apparatus that they built,

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.450
that let them raise

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.420
the denominator of their fraction.

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:14.790
So without changing the amount

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:16.320
of heavy metals coming out,

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:20.410
the bottom half of that
got higher and higher

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:23.550
as they put online this new system.

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:25.020
And now it's almost impossible

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:26.940
to tell if they have any heavy metals

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:27.890
going out the door.

00:06:32.670 --> 00:06:34.000
The company is very straightforward.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:34.857
We asked them,

00:06:34.857 --> 00:06:36.900
"Have you reduced the
amount of heavy metals?"

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:37.733
And they said,

00:06:37.733 --> 00:06:38.737
"No, nothing that we've done

00:06:38.737 --> 00:06:40.137
"reduces the concentrations,

00:06:40.137 --> 00:06:42.760
"increases the concentrations, unchanged."

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:44.220
But what they have done

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:46.833
is accounted for water differently.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:49.890
In an email exchange with us,

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:52.860
the company asserted
that the Italian court

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:55.273
never determined that the
crimes were committed.

00:06:56.721 --> 00:06:58.470
A really key turning point

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:01.570
was getting the paperwork from the court,

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:03.700
which we were able to
make a special request

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:05.030
by citing public interest

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:06.590
in our status as journalists,

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:08.770
to get the actual documentation

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:11.080
of what happened in court that day.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:12.110
And it says by how much,

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:14.350
mercury limit was exceeded

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:17.623
by six times over, 50% over, 30% over.

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:21.400
That having these raw numbers

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:22.233
and then going back

00:07:22.233 --> 00:07:23.120
and seeing it's never been

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:26.050
in any of their filings to shareholders.

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:27.620
They've never described it that way.

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:29.420
They don't really ever talk about it

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:32.170
and seemed like it kind
of an important moment

00:07:32.170 --> 00:07:34.569
and so, we knew that we were seeing

00:07:34.569 --> 00:07:36.040
a difference between

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:37.620
what was being presented to the public,

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:39.600
being presented to investors

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.150
and the hard documentation,

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:42.440
and that hard documentation

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:44.303
had never come out before.

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:46.170
The idea that this

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:48.530
is going on 365 days a year

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:50.020
with no attempt to hide it.

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:51.370
There's no wall behind

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:52.550
which you need to peer.

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:54.670
There's no boundaries around this trench

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:56.100
that literally goes into the sea.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:57.160
And in the summers,

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:58.370
I've seen it with my own eyes,

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:00.030
there are people literally bathing

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:01.680
right on the ditch,

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:05.300
right where the discharge enters the sea.

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:07.110
The water is a little bit warmer,

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:08.430
perhaps that's what attracts

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:09.730
some of the bathers.

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:11.720
And the community that
lives around this plant

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:14.653
has elevated levels of diseases.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:21.940
Showing causality, always difficult.

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:24.040
But there is a lot that the activists

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:25.560
have gotten their teeth into

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:27.663
about showing that there is an impact.

00:09:30.612 --> 00:09:32.740
Activists have described the attitude

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:34.190
here as resignation.

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:35.610
Some people don't want to know what's,

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:38.370
you know, in the air and in the soil.

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:39.790
We spoke to some of the residents,

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:41.660
most of whom were rather

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:43.170
indifferent to the plant,

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:44.970
even the lady who lives right

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:46.890
on the footsteps of the plant

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:47.940
sort of shrugged her shoulders

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:50.490
and said, "You know, you've
gotta die of something."

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:52.171
And when we made our way

00:09:52.171 --> 00:09:53.800
to the plant's entrance,

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:56.563
well, the reception
there was quite frosty.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.960
We came here and security

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:01.080
at the front gate of the plant

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:03.650
stopped Elisa because
she was taking pictures

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:05.880
and they threatened to call the police.

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:07.730
And so she joked this morning that,

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:09.360
you know, be careful
when the police stop you

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:11.270
so they don't break your cameras.

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:14.060
Sure enough, when we were
filming our interview

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:15.888
with an activist on the beach,

00:10:15.888 --> 00:10:18.280
men in plain clothes came up behind us

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:19.113
when we were done,

00:10:19.113 --> 00:10:19.946
flashed their badges

00:10:19.946 --> 00:10:20.850
and wanted to see ID,

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:22.700
and wanted to know who
we were working for.

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:24.200
You don't get close to this plant

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:26.090
without somebody knowing who you are,

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:29.070
what you're doing and making you feel

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:30.896
a little uncomfortable about being here.

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:39.730
I think the trouble
with the regulation is,

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:40.780
as we found,

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:42.678
is in part the disjointed nature.

00:10:42.678 --> 00:10:44.942
On the one hand, you have the courts,

00:10:44.942 --> 00:10:47.600
they enforce the law, they prosecute.

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:48.433
On the other hand,

00:10:48.433 --> 00:10:50.210
you have the environment ministry,

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:52.872
which is now in charge of regulating

00:10:52.872 --> 00:10:57.270
and allowing Solvay to operate a plant.

00:10:57.270 --> 00:10:58.510
It wasn't clear to us

00:10:58.510 --> 00:10:59.700
just how much communication

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:01.210
there was between for example,

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:03.470
the courts and the environment ministry.

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:04.670
We know that prosecutors

00:11:04.670 --> 00:11:06.170
are looking at Solvay again,

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:08.260
though it's not clear what the basis

00:11:08.260 --> 00:11:09.810
of their investigation might be,

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:13.873
how advanced and who it
might be focusing on.

00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:19.783
So you've launched

00:11:19.783 --> 00:11:21.700
a pretty high profile campaign

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:24.330
to get the CEO of Solvay removed.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:25.700
Another important turning point

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:28.220
was the entry onto the scene of Bluebell,

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:29.520
an activist investor group

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:30.700
based in London.

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:31.533
And you know,

00:11:31.533 --> 00:11:33.330
every year they pick another target

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:34.230
and buy one share.

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:35.063
In this case,

00:11:35.063 --> 00:11:36.650
they bought one share of Solvay

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:38.500
and they went after the company for its,

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:39.683
for its Italian plant.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:50.310
And what this did was create

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:51.940
a ton of publicity around this

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:53.350
and raised some really good questions.

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:54.840
And what caught our eye

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:58.800
was at the 2021 shareholders meeting.

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:00.010
They asked a lot of questions

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:01.160
about the water flowing in,

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:02.846
the water flowing out.

00:12:02.846 --> 00:12:05.400
And they didn't get a lot of answers.

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:07.300
They got a lot of apples and oranges

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:08.890
figures from the company.

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:10.308
Companies certainly didn't tell them

00:12:10.308 --> 00:12:11.400
what they could have,

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:12.580
which was that they had changed

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:14.030
how they account for the water

00:12:14.030 --> 00:12:15.853
starting in 2019.

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:21.320
What happens next is Solvay

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:23.350
is facing a litany of challenges.

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:26.558
They're facing it with
a potential prosecution

00:12:26.558 --> 00:12:27.960
in the Livorno courts.

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:30.050
They're facing it with an uprising

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:32.120
from this activist investor.

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:33.830
They're facing it from activists

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:35.320
who are energized by the fact

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:37.000
that some had no idea

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:38.120
that the government here in Italy

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:39.660
was about to renew their license

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:40.860
for another 12 years.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.770
And that renewal there

00:12:42.770 --> 00:12:43.860
is really important to them

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:45.030
and staying in business here,

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:47.310
and being viable and not having found

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:48.950
to have violated any laws

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:50.710
or have problems with disclosure.

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:53.460
They need everything to go right for them.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:54.790
Not just because this is,

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.060
you know, 17% of their global business

00:12:57.060 --> 00:12:59.800
and one that they wanna
sell or dispose of,

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:02.230
but because it could affect their stock.

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:03.780
I mean, always you can see it,

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:05.969
the fact that they're pushing back

00:13:05.969 --> 00:13:06.970
against this activist investor

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:08.210
and trying to discredit him

00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:10.000
with public statements.

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:12.050
This is a turning point for this company.

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:16.684
As things stand there are no indications

00:13:16.684 --> 00:13:19.670
that Solvay intends to change this process

00:13:19.670 --> 00:13:21.307
in this particular location.

00:13:21.307 --> 00:13:23.360
And the change will probably

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:24.730
have to come from above.

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:25.810
The change will probably have

00:13:25.810 --> 00:13:29.210
to come from policy that is updated

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:31.570
to reflect the norms and practices

00:13:31.570 --> 00:13:33.763
that are used elsewhere.

00:13:34.610 --> 00:13:37.100
But it is astounding that no matter

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:38.850
what is being discharged,

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:39.967
the sheer volume of it,

00:13:39.967 --> 00:13:41.500
and the fact that it's affecting

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:43.830
the landscape is carrying on

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:45.860
and has been carrying on for decades.

